WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.321
You don't need to be a Supreme Kai to know
how much of an influence the Dragon Ball Z

00:00:04.321 --> 00:00:06.070
series has had on the world.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:09.660
But there's a lot more to this franchise than
just fast fights, spiky hair, and screaming

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.049
at the top of your lungs.

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:16.280
With over $5 billion in franchise sales, DBZ
is a cornerstone of Japanese animation and

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.400
a cultural phenomenon, and the tale of Goku
and friends has had more twists and turns

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.720
than Snake Way.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.859
Despite its impact, DBZ is only one part of
the story.

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:30.160
The Dragon Ball franchise has spawned four
original series, 19 movies, over 500 chapters

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.950
of manga, nearly 100 video games, and all
kinds of ridiculous memes and debates about

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.090
power levels.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.920
So take a break from your training, take a
bite out of a senzu bean, and take a Grand

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.379
Tour with us through the untold truth of Dragon
Ball Z.

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:45.379
Dragon Boy

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:50.620
You might think Goku's story began with Akira
Toriyama's first Dragon Ball manga in a 1984

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.809
issue of Weekly Shonen Jump, but his origins
start way before that.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:59.539
Toriyama, who'd already won multiple awards
for his hit comedy manga Dr. Slump, wanted

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:02.320
to do something drastically different for
his next project.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.409
Mixing together sexual humor and early '80s
Jackie Chan-esque action-comedy, Toriyama

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:11.930
made the manga Dragon Boy, which served as
a short prototype to the Dragon Ball story.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:17.130
A year later, Toriyama started a new Shonen
Jump manga series with Dragon Boy as its jumping-off

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.140
point, and the rest is history — literally.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.729
Journey to the West

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:26.960
For inspiration in turning Dragon Boy to the
long-running Dragon Ball, Toriyama and his

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.320
team turned to older folklore, in particular
the 16th century novel Journey to the West.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.140
The story featured the inspirations for Son
Goku, the Power Pole weapon, the Flying Nimbus

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.969
cloud, Bulma, Oolong the shapeshifting pig,
Yamcha the desert bandit, the Ox King, and

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.700
his castle on a fiery hill.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.450
According to Toriyama's editor, Kazuhiko Torishima,
using these details to help hang the story

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.460
on was a matter of convenience.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.600
As Torishima puts it, adding elements from
Journey to the West to the Dragon Boy story

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.600
was his idea.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.730
He says, "The biggest reason for that was
it was a free intellectual property, as it

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:01.730
was very old.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:05.590
In addition, when you need to make a long
running manga series, you need to add a lot

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:10.270
more features [...] So when we moved Dragon
Boy to a long running story format, that's

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.720
when the Journey to the West elements came
in."

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.090
The idea of gathering the seven dragon balls
to summon Shenron the wish-granting Eternal

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:22.860
Dragon was heavily inspired by the early 1800s
novel Nansō Satomi Hakkenden, also known

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.080
as The Eight Dogs Chronicles.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:29.530
Hakkenden's story depicted a princess who
gave birth to eight crystal balls after getting

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.580
freaky with a dog.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.660
The crystal balls then flew into the sky and
scattered across the world, just like the

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.420
dragon balls do after a wish, but became people
instead.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.160
Considering the world of Dragon Ball features
all kinds of anthropomorphic animals, the

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.160
inspiration is pretty clear.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.530
Good thing they left out most of the gross
stuff.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:48.940
Goku grows up

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.910
When enthusiasm for Dragon Ball began to dwindle,
Torishima and Toriyama decided to drastically

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.370
change things, putting Goku on a quest to
become the strongest person ever, and the

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.870
series' emphasis shifted from comedy to action.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.190
As a result, the final arc of Dragon Ball
was the Piccolo Jr. saga, which featured the

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.670
most intense fights of the series.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:08.950
Goku was growing up.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.060
Engagement with Dragon Ball spiked during
the action-filled final saga, leaving fans

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.620
clamoring for a continuation of the story.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.130
Torishima later spoke about how they came
up with the title.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:24.230
"I went and asked Toriyama for his input and
he answered immediately by saying 'Dragon

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.960
Ball Z … because this is last, nothing comes
after this.'"

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.670
DBZ was meant to be the end for Goku's story
— multiple times, usually with him passing

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.110
the torch to another hero.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.830
Initially, the Frieza saga was meant to be
the final chapter, which shouldn’t surprise

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.120
anyone who’s seen it.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.110
In that story, the franchise's longest fight,
Goku beats the strongest, most evil character

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.940
in the universe and ascends to an unbeatable
form.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.500
The planet-ending saga was so epic it seemed
like a natural conclusion, but there would

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.920
still be a long way to go and many more transformations
before the series truly came to an end.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.520
East meets west (and vice versa)

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.060
What does a franchise do when its creative
team runs out of ideas?

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.630
Go to space or travel through time — and
DBZ did both.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:12.070
As the Super Saiyan success story continued,
Toriyama kept introducing more Western tropes.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:16.570
Goku's alien backstory, abnormal strength,
and alien heritage was inspired by the lore

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.780
of Superman.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:23.400
Goku (Superman) landed on Earth as a baby
and was raised like any other human.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.680
He grew to fight members of his nearly-extinct
race trying to conquer Earth.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.680
More story turns inspired by western media
include the outer space adventure to Namek,

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.610
which was largely influenced by Star Wars,
as well as the following Android saga, which

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.280
took inspiration from the Terminator movies.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:44.060
Terminator 2: Judgment Day hit theaters in
July 1991 — by November of that year, DBZ

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.630
started a story arc featuring a badass guy
going back through time, trying to prevent

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:51.340
an apocalyptic future where cyborgs exterminated
humanity.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.510
It helps explain why the series became such
an international phenomenon — its influenced

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:59.240
by enduring stories from all over the world.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.950
Censorship and controversies

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:05.480
As the series entered the North American market,
a lot of changes were made in the translation,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.300
mostly to make the series come off as more
kid-friendly.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.320
All instances of death, heaven, and hell were
altered.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:15.960
Vegeta wasn't "killing" Frieza's men — he
was simply sending them to the "next dimension."

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.130
The shirts on the ogres living there reading
"HELL" were partially censored to look like

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.540
the letters "HFIL”, standing for the "Home
For Infinite Losers."

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:29.420
Mr. Satan's name was changed to Hercule, and
scenes of cigarettes, blood, alcohol, nudity,

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.050
and middle fingers were all removed.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.480
Changes have continued with re-airings of
the show on different networks, such as when

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:40.550
The CW changed up Mr. Popo’s look to make
him look less like a jarring blackface caricature.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:44.890
We get the idea, but it kind of just makes
Mr. Popo look like a weirdly racist Genie

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:45.890
from Aladdin.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:51.120
(Genie singing in stereotyped accents)

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.880
Evolution, god-battles, resurrection, and
beyond

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.830
After Dragon Ball Z ended in 1996, Toei Animation
wanted to continue the series due to its widespread

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:01.830
success.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:06.139
As a result, Dragon Ball GT was created by
Toei's staff without any input from Toriyama

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:07.990
except for the series' name.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:12.500
GT kept Goku's story going, but it was met
with negative reviews, failing to live up

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.190
to its predecessor without Toriyama at the
helm.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:20.780
Save a few specials and movies, Dragon Ball
GT's final 1997 episode was the last time

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:25.450
television viewers in Japan would get to see
Goku and the gang for a long time.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.940
During this time, Dragon Ball Z was just starting
to take off in North America.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:33.580
When the episodes ran out, Dragon Ball was
spun off into the live-action Dragonball Evolution,

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.140
loosely based on the original Dragon Ball
story.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.960
It’s... not a great adaptation.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.580
"Meet Lord Piccolo.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:44.960
He'll take on anyone to unleash his vengeance
on the world."

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.720
"I can't stand it!

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:48.860
Ugh!"

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:54.380
Toei tested the waters for the franchise's
return in 2009 with Dragon Ball Kai, a redubbed,

00:06:54.389 --> 00:06:57.840
whittled-down version of DBZ with updated
animation.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.070
The success of that series led to a revival
of the franchise, with Toriyama returning

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:06.290
for 2013's successful Dragon Ball Z: Battle
of Gods movie.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:10.960
In its home country, it was a big deal — the
movie opened at the top of the Japanese box

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.450
office, and made its mark as the first Japanese
film to ever screen in IMAX.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:19.539
The movie's critical and commercial success
opened the door for something fans never expected

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:22.740
— a whole new series, Dragon Ball Super.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:25.200
So what's next for the Dragon Ball franchise?

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.740
Only time - and Goku's fists of fury - will
tell.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:29.740
Thanks for watching!

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.510
